            <ArticleTitle>Comparing drugs for short-term sedation.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>55-60</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Selected benzodiazepines and a phenol derivative are reviewed in relation to their appropriateness as short-term sedatives in settings such as noninvasive and invasive medical procedures. Terminating sedation with flumazenil is also a focus of interest.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
